## File 2: product-reviews-star-rating.liquid

```liquid
{% comment %}
  Product Reviews Star Rating Display
  ===================================
  
  A lightweight, accessible star rating component that displays aggregate
  review data stored in product metafields.
  
  @param {product} product - Required. The product object to display ratings for
  @param {boolean} show_count - Show review count next to stars (default: true)
  @param {boolean} show_empty - Show empty stars when no reviews exist (default: false)
  @param {string} size - Star size: 'small', 'medium', 'large' (default: 'medium')
  @param {string} color_filled - CSS color for filled stars (default: '#fbbf24')
  @param {string} color_empty - CSS color for empty stars (default: '#d1d5db')
  @param {boolean} link_to_reviews - Link to reviews section on click (default: true)
  @param {boolean} schema_enabled - Output JSON-LD structured data (default: true)
  
  Usage:
    {% render 'product-reviews-star-rating', product: product %}
    {% render 'product-reviews-star-rating', product: product, size: 'small', show_count: false %}
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  PARAMETER DEFAULTS
  We use the | default filter to establish sensible defaults while allowing
  complete override flexibility. This pattern ensures the snippet works
  out-of-the-box while remaining highly configurable.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign show_count = show_count | default: true
  assign show_empty = show_empty | default: false
  assign size = size | default: 'medium'
  assign color_filled = color_filled | default: '#fbbf24'
  assign color_empty = color_empty | default: '#d1d5db'
  assign link_to_reviews = link_to_reviews | default: true
  assign schema_enabled = schema_enabled | default: true
-%}

{% comment %}
  METAFIELD DATA EXTRACTION
  We support multiple metafield access patterns to ensure compatibility
  across different theme configurations and Shopify versions.
  
  Priority order:
  1. Direct metafield access (OS 2.0 style)
  2. Metafields array access (legacy style)
  3. Default to 0 if no data exists
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  # Try OS 2.0 direct access first, then fall back to legacy access
  assign rating_average = product.metafields.reviews.rating_average.value | default: product.metafields.reviews.rating_average | default: 0
  assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: product.metafields.reviews.rating_count | default: 0
  
  # Convert to numbers and ensure valid ranges
  assign rating_average = rating_average | plus: 0
  assign rating_count = rating_count | plus: 0
  
  # Clamp rating between 0 and 5 for safety
  if rating_average > 5
    assign rating_average = 5
  endif
  if rating_average < 0
    assign rating_average = 0
  endif
  
  # Determine if we should render anything
  assign has_reviews = false
  if rating_count > 0 and rating_average > 0
    assign has_reviews = true
  endif
  
  # Early exit conditions
  assign should_render = has_reviews
  if show_empty
    assign should_render = true
  endif
-%}

{% comment %}
  EARLY EXIT
  If there are no reviews and show_empty is false, we exit early
  to avoid rendering unnecessary DOM elements.
{% endcomment %}
{%- unless should_render -%}
  {%- break -%}
{%- endunless -%}

{% comment %}
  STAR CALCULATION
  We calculate the number of full stars, half stars, and empty stars.
  This uses integer math to avoid floating point issues in Liquid.
  
  Example: 4.3 rating
  - Full stars: 4 (floor of 4.3)
  - Decimal: 0.3 (4.3 - 4)
  - Half star: No (0.3 < 0.25 threshold for half)
  - Empty stars: 1 (5 - 4 - 0)
  
  Example: 4.7 rating
  - Full stars: 4 (floor of 4.7)
  - Decimal: 0.7 (4.7 - 4)
  - Half star: Yes (0.7 >= 0.25)
  - Empty stars: 0 (5 - 4 - 1)
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  # Calculate star distribution
  assign rating_floor = rating_average | floor
  assign rating_decimal = rating_average | minus: rating_floor | times: 100 | round
  
  # Determine if we need a half star (threshold: 0.25 to 0.75)
  assign has_half_star = false
  if rating_decimal >= 25 and rating_decimal < 75
    assign has_half_star = true
  endif
  
  # If decimal is >= 0.75, round up to full star
  assign full_stars = rating_floor
  if rating_decimal >= 75
    assign full_stars = full_stars | plus: 1
  endif
  
  # Calculate empty stars
  assign filled_count = full_stars
  if has_half_star
    assign filled_count = filled_count | plus: 1
  endif
  assign empty_stars = 5 | minus: filled_count
  
  # Ensure we don't exceed 5 stars total
  if empty_stars < 0
    assign empty_stars = 0
  endif
-%}

{% comment %}
  SIZE CONFIGURATION
  We use size presets that scale well across different viewport sizes.
  The sizes are based on common UI patterns and accessibility guidelines
  (minimum touch target of 44px for interactive elements).
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  case size
    when 'small'
      assign star_size = '14px'
      assign font_size = '12px'
      assign gap_size = '2px'
    when 'large'
      assign star_size = '24px'
      assign font_size = '16px'
      assign gap_size = '4px'
    else
      # Default: medium
      assign star_size = '18px'
      assign font_size = '14px'
      assign gap_size = '3px'
  endcase
-%}

{% comment %}
  UNIQUE ID GENERATION
  We generate a unique ID for this instance to scope our CSS and enable
  proper ARIA relationships. This allows multiple instances on the same page.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign unique_id = 'star-rating-' | append: product.id | append: '-' | append: 'now' | date: '%N' -%}

{% comment %}
  ACCESSIBILITY TEXT
  We build comprehensive accessible text that screen readers will announce.
  This follows WCAG 2.1 guidelines for non-text content.
{% endcomment %}
{%- capture aria_label -%}
  {%- if has_reviews -%}
    {{ rating_average }} out of 5 stars based on {{ rating_count }} {{ rating_count | pluralize: 'review', 'reviews' }}
  {%- else -%}
    No reviews yet
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{% comment %}
  REVIEW COUNT TEXT
  We pluralize the review count text properly for grammatical correctness.
{% endcomment %}
{%- capture review_text -%}
  {%- if rating_count == 1 -%}
    1 review
  {%- else -%}
    {{ rating_count }} reviews
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{% comment %}
  SCOPED STYLES
  We output scoped CSS inline to avoid external dependencies and ensure
  the component works immediately after insertion. The styles use CSS
  custom properties for easy theming and are scoped to avoid conflicts.
{% endcomment %}
